### 1.2 Mandatory UI / Client Runtime Checks (`A5`, `A4`)
For every UI workflow in the plan, verify:
1. **Real UI States (`A5`)**: Trigger and capture `loading`, `empty`, `error` (validation + server error), and `populated` states against the live runtime.
2. **Role & Capability Visibility (`A5`)**: Log in using separate isolated sessions per role (`{{roles}}`) and confirm unauthorized actions/navigation items are absent or disabled as specified.
3. **Environment / Scope Switching (`A5`)**: When switching tenant/organization/environment (`{{scope_list}}`), confirm data views and active caches refetch the new scope without stale cross-scope leakage.
4. **Reload Persistence (`A4`)**: After any mutation, reload the screen/view and verify the updated state renders from persisted storage.
5. **Console & Network Health (`A5`)**: Inspect console and network logs after every flow. Any new uncaught exception, framework hydration error, or unexpected `4xx`/`5xx` response outside documented baseline noise (`{{baseline_noise}}`) fails the case (`FAIL`).

