## 2. API / Service Surface Execution & Security Hand-Off (`A6`, `SR14`)

Primary tool: **{{api_tool}}** (fallback: `{{api_fallback}}`) · Service base: `{{api_base_url}}`

### 2.1 Functional, Persistence & Side-Effect Checks (`A4`, `A6`)
For every API/service case:
- **Status & Contract**: Verify HTTP/RPC status code, response schema, error envelope structure, and pagination/filtering invariants.
- **Persistence Read-Back (`A4`)**: Follow every `POST`/`PUT`/`PATCH`/`DELETE` (or command mutation) with a `GET` (or state query) to confirm persisted fields and timestamps.
- **Asynchronous Side Effects (`A6`)**: Verify background jobs, emitted domain events, audit log records (`actor`, `tenant_id`, `action`), and cache invalidation triggered by the operation.
- **Idempotency & Concurrency (`A6`)**: Replay mutating requests with the same idempotency key or duplicate submission to confirm safe deduplication or conflict (`409` / `422`) handling.

### 2.2 Live Permission Matrix & `security-review` (`SR14`) Runtime Verification (`A6`)

UI hiding never proves access control. Execute direct API/service calls across the workspace's **`Role × Environment × Action × Object`** matrix and any runtime-dependent **`PLAUSIBLE`** checks handed over by `security-review` (`SR14`, {{security_review_link}}):

| Matrix Scenario | Caller Identity & Role (`{{roles}}`) | Target Scope (`{{scope_list}}`) | Expected Status & Behavior | Runtime Evidence (`{{evidence_path}}`) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Unauthenticated Call** | No token / expired token | Any protected endpoint | `401 Unauthorized` (zero state change) | Redacted response capture |
| **Insufficient Role (BFLA)** | Lower-privilege role calling privileged mutation | Own `{{scope_list}}` | `403 Forbidden` (zero state change) | Redacted response + read-back proving no mutation |
| **Cross-Scope / Anti-IDOR (BOLA)** | Authenticated role in Tenant/Owner A | Resource owned by Tenant/Owner B | `404 Not Found` or `403 Forbidden` (zero data leak) | Redacted response + read-back on Tenant B resource |
| **`security-review` `PLAUSIBLE` Hand-Off (`SR14`)** | Scenario specified in `{{security_report_location}}` | Target boundary from `SR14` | Disprove exploit (`PASS`) or confirm exploit (`FAIL` → `BLOCKER`) | Full request/response trace returned to Security Review |

